Subject: [PATCH 1/3] vk_query_cache: bound the running occlusion query across
 submissions

Since the counter is paused instead of reset at each submission, the host
query runs until the guest resets or reports the counter. Ocarina of
Time's title screen and file select keep ZPass counting on and do
neither, so the query grew by a slot at every submission and render
pass. By the time gameplay started it held 16,384 slots over all 64
sample banks, and a running query keeps every bank it touches alive. On
AMD with EDEN_NX2_SPLIT=2 the game then hung right after picking the
save, with WaitSubmitted waiting on a tick the GPU thread never
submitted (reported on zortos293/Lichii#121).

Once the running query passes one bank (256 slots), drop the count as a
reset would. In gameplay the longest reset-to-report window measured was
36 slots over 4 submissions (1.36M reports), so real windows keep the
carried count.

Tested on RTX 4090, Low accuracy, EDEN_NX2_SPLIT=2,
EDEN_NX2_FENCE_BATCH=1. With logging on, the query stayed within two
banks through the title screen and file select, and gameplay windows
were unchanged. Outside Link's house, 36 s of consecutive frames with
Link on screen: 0 flashes in 576 frames, 60.5 fps.
tests.exe: 651 of 654 pass, the same 3 known failures as before. The
hang itself doesn't reproduce on NVIDIA, so the AMD retest is pending.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 47e1e95208490cbcf0e036505ec23ba7f033b0ff)
(cherry picked from commit 87203d5936d6b1c26f54ea83829c941a37a3ddfc)
---
 src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_query_cache.cpp | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_query_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_query_cache.cpp
index 4b8161a30d..e7c965ca02 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_query_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_query_cache.cpp
@@ -210,8 +210,17 @@ public:
         last_accumulation_checkpoint = (std::max)(last_accumulation_checkpoint, num_slots_used);
     }
 
+    // Called at each submission. The running query carries the count across it: a guest's
+    // reset-to-report window can span one.
     void CloseCounter() override {
         PauseCounter();
+        // A title that counts without resetting or reporting grows the query by a slot at every
+        // submission and render pass, and the query keeps every bank it touches alive. Ocarina of
+        // Time's title screen and file select reached 16,384 slots over 64 banks (its gameplay
+        // windows span at most 36 slots). Past a bank, drop the count as a reset would.
+        if (current_query && current_query->size_slots > SamplesQueryBank::BANK_SIZE) {
+            ResetCounter();
+        }
     }
 
     bool HasPendingSync() const override {
